# First Delivery

<!-- page: ii -->

The crate came in on a Tuesday and sat by the door <!-- page: 1 -->until somebody signed for it\.

<!-- page: 2 -->

<!-- textmouth-heading: eyJsZXZlbCI6MiwidGV4dCI6Ik9wZW5pbmcgdGhlIENyYXRlIn0= -->

## Opening the Crate

Inside lay a brass tele<!-- page: 3 -->phone and a coil of cable\.

<!-- page: 3 -->

The coil was wound tight and its label was smudged\.

Someone had pencilled a note in the margin\.

<!-- chapter: Second Delivery -->
# Second Delivery

<!-- page: 4 -->

The second crate held only straw and a receipt\.